{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210393-how-will-the-realm-3rd-edition-book-be-different-than-previous-editions","id":1210393,"title":"How will The Realm 3rd edition book be different than previous editions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-23T06:56:54-07:00","id":1210393,"title":"How will The Realm 3rd edition book be different than previous editions?","content":"Hello all. I\u2019m trying to decide if it is worth getting the realm book as an add on for the DB Kickstarter. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7142-streetunderbamboo","name":"StreetUnderBamboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T07:06:28-07:00","id":1210397,"title":"","content":"It includes a revised presentation of the Blessed Isle's prefectures, with an eye towards making the Isle a fun and exciting venue for play, even if you're not playing Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Unlike Second Edition's Compass: Blessed Isle, it includes write-ups of the Realm's satrapies across Creation, both new and old.<br /> <br /> It includes material that's unique to Third Edition, such as the Caul and the groundwork of the War in the West.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T07:09:35-07:00","id":1210398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StreetUnderBamboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210393-how-will-the-realm-3rd-edition-book-be-different-than-previous-editions#post1210393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all. I\u2019m trying to decide if it is worth getting the realm book as an add on for the DB Kickstarter. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what what they\u2019ve released a lot of the structure is intact, but there significant changes (in my opinion) to various organizations such as the Immaculate Order\u2019s view of Solar Abe Linar Anathema. Additionally, they are giving depth to a lot of the Realm satrapies and even portions of the blessed isle that are new and engaging.<br /> <br /> These are my thoughts but the Devs seems to be doing a kick ass job on the world building adding to the richness of creation with the added benefit of not removing all of previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:21:54-07:00","id":1210450,"title":"","content":"I think making the Realm more varied and interesting is useful (2nd ed Realm was pretty bland), but having a bunch of Satrapies I think is the main change. So it's got locations from every direction, rather than just the Blessed Isle itself.<br /> <br /> Also, most of the Satrapies seem to be new stuff, so it's not like those 2nd ed Compasses that spent a lot of time talking about places you already know about. (I really liked the second half of 2e Compass: The North, but the first half was basically just a reprint of Bastions of the North with a few changes in the detail. Same with Lookshy, the Lintha, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T10:31:02-07:00","id":1210480,"title":"","content":"It could just be that previous editions didn't lure me in properly enough, but even just from the descriptions in WFHW, it made the disparate parts of the Blessed Isle seem, well, disparate. I literally never once saw, heard of, or played a game set on the Blessed Isle, beyond maybe the Imperial City. I think this was because the entire island was mainly billed as &quot;preternaturally climate and prodigious breadbasket, but also there is a giant mountain.&quot;<br /> <br /> This time though, their is actual Geography, and history, and it is varied from coast to coast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T11:23:15-07:00","id":1210498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210393-how-will-the-realm-3rd-edition-book-be-different-than-previous-editions?p=1210480#post1210480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could just be that previous editions didn't lure me in properly enough, but even just from the descriptions in WFHW, it made the disparate parts of the Blessed Isle seem, well, disparate. I literally never once saw, heard of, or played a game set on the Blessed Isle, beyond maybe the Imperial City. I think this was because the entire island was mainly billed as &quot;preternaturally climate and prodigious breadbasket, but also there is a giant mountain.&quot;<br /> <br /> This time though, their is actual Geography, and history, and it is varied from coast to coast.</div> </div> </div> </div>We had bits there. But mostly the setting was &quot;some DBs' manor&quot; or once, a war-manse. That was it. Certainly even DB games spent most of their time outside it.<br /> <br /> Oh, there was the one time we hunted Ragara, who'd turned himself into a ten-mile-long nuclear-cancer-dragon and was marauding across the Realm's countryside spreading death and pestilence... but that could have happened anywhere.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the game was sometimes set there for various reasons, but besides it being the DB's home base, not really because of it being an interesting place in of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-23-2018, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:12:29-07:00","id":1211115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210393-how-will-the-realm-3rd-edition-book-be-different-than-previous-editions?p=1210398#post1210398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">such as the Immaculate Order\u2019s view of Solar Abe Linar Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Abe Linar Anathema is going to be my next Solar NPC. He'll have a huge beard, no shirt, and murder the undead with an axe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:40:49-07:00","id":1211135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210393-how-will-the-realm-3rd-edition-book-be-different-than-previous-editions?p=1211115#post1211115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solar Abe Linar Anathema is going to be my next Solar NPC. He'll have a huge beard, no shirt, and murder the undead with an axe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I...got nothing, well played all I can say is autocorrect does the strangest things...&gt;.&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}